# Note: to make our life easier, we now sync every change from the upstream
# maintainance branch(release/${VER}/master) into AOSC-Tracking with the
# UPSTREAM: tag when we update core minor version or patch level.  Assuming
# the remote referring to the upstream repo is "origin" and the one
# referring to AOSC-Tracking is "aosc" in your glibc git repo, it can be
# done via:
#
# git fetch origin
# git fetch aosc
# git branch -D aosc/glibc-${VER}
# git checkout aosc/glibc-${VER}
# git tag rebase_basepoint
# git rebase origin/release/${VER}/master
# GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR=vim GIT_EDITOR="sed -i -e '1s/^/UPSTREAM: /'" \
# git rebase rebase_basepoint -i
#
# Then change "pick" to "reword" for everything in the upstream maintainance
# branch in vim (or your preferred editor, set it via GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR)
# and put the lines for them earlier than other changes.
#
# Also update the aosc/${VER}-ow branch for runtime-emulation/liblol
# similarly.
